     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, I am looking for a better way to get <span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,serif;font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);line-height:16.666667938232422px\">geom_boxplot</span><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,serif;font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);line-height:16.666667938232422px\">() </span>to zoom in automatically when it encounters a uniform sample. In many thousands of data sets, my program occasionally encounters samples of (e.g.) mercury from several stations, with all samples containing the identical measurement.  The resulting ggplot2 plot of grouped boxplots (identical median) produces a y range that extends into the negatives, which is impossible for this kind of data.  I want it to do the same as base R, that is, zoom in automatically.  Here is a sample for a single station of this type: <br><div><pre style=\"margin-bottom:10px;padding:5px;font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,serif;overflow:auto;width:auto;max-height:600px;color:rgb(0,0,0);line-height:16.666667938232422px\"><code style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">dput</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">df</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">)</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">\r\n\r\nstructure</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">list</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">station </span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">=</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\"> structure</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">c</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(128,0,0)\">1L</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">,</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(128,0,0)\">1L</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">,</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(128,0,0)\">1L</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\">,</span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:13.333333969116211px;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(128,0,0)\">1L</span><spa